invariant: INV-17
file: ct_wipe.c
catches: test/lint-runtime-symbols.sh
reason: ct_wipe stores its whole words through an lvalue that is not
  volatile. Every byte is still zero, so no vector notices, but a hosted
  compile at -O2 reads the loop as a fill and writes a call to memset in
  its place, the call docs/decisions.md 144 removed. Inlined at the end of
  a caller, those stores are ones the compiler may delete as no later read
  needs them. lint-runtime-symbols holds ct_wipe.c to no call at all on
  arm64 and x86-64.

--- old
        ((volatile ct_wipe_word *)(byte + head))[i] = 0;
--- new
        ((ct_wipe_word *)(byte + head))[i] = 0;
